// Test: bugfixes/callcapability_empty_vtable_emits_unreachable
// Grammar: capability_decl · method_call on capability-typed param
// Semantic: An in-scope `can Cap:` declaration + a function that accepts
//   a Cap-typed parameter and dispatches to a Cap method (via
//   `param.method()`) MUST compile even when no class in the current
//   build claims `can Cap`. The generated dispatch site is provably
//   unreachable — there is no receiver value whose runtime class-id
//   would match any arm — so codegen emits WASM `unreachable`. The
//   receiver-typed argument site is separately blocked by the resolver's
//   SEM011 conformance check whenever a caller actually tries to pass a
//   class-typed value to a Cap-typed parameter of a non-conforming class.
//
// Before 0.33.113 the compiler failed with the internal assertion
//   "CallCapability: no class conforms to capability #N slot 0 —
//    resolver should have prevented this"
//   which fired at codegen time. The assertion was correct in spirit
//   (an unreachable code path snuck through codegen) but wrong in
//   response — the correct emission is `unreachable`, not an assertion.
//
// Reported context: frame.data v3.0.12 emits
//   `class Database` with `save(Persist target)` whose body dispatches
//   to `target.save()`. When user code declares `data Widget:` but not
//   `class Widget can Persist`, the vtable for Persist is empty. Every
//   Database.save/delete/deleteAll body then trips this codegen path.
//   Team-prompt d227e2be asks frame.data v3.0.13 to emit the class-side
//   `cans:["Persist"]` claim so the vtable is populated for user code
//   that actually calls those methods.
//
// This pin covers the WORST case: capability declared, capability-typed
//   helper method exists, NO conforming class. Verifies:
//   (a) compilation succeeds
//   (b) start: runs to completion without ever reaching the dead branch
//   (c) the runtime does NOT trap (proves the unreachable arm is truly
//       unreachable in this specific execution)
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.113
//
// Expected output:
//   compiled

start:
	// Deliberately do NOT construct any Persist-conforming value.
	// The `helper` function body compiles to an unreachable-arm
	// dispatch, but start: never invokes helper, so no trap fires.
	print("compiled")

can Persist:
	boolean save()

functions:
	boolean helper(Persist target)
		return target.save()
